"\n"
"Screens to read barcodes on stock operations with a barcode scanner (USB\n"
"or Bluetooth scanners typing the barcode followed by Enter) or typing\n"
"them, on desktop and mobile browsers: receipts, deliveries, internal\n"
"transfers, relocations, batch transfers, unplanned transfers and\n"
"inventory counts. No Odoo Enterprise license is required.\n"
"\n"
"All the logic lives in ``stock_capture``, shared with the other capture\n"
"screens (e.g. the weighing screens of ``stock_weighing``); this module\n"
"adds the screens, the barcode main menu and the buttons to open them.\n"
"\n"
"**Table of contents**\n"
"\n"
".. contents::\n"
"   :local:\n"
"\n"
"Configuration\n"
"=============\n"
"\n"
"Before configuring, analyze with the people doing them the flow of each\n"
"operation: what is read and in which order, what the screen must propose\n"
"and what it must refuse. Then adjust a capture profile to each flow\n"
"(*Inventory > Configuration > Capture Profiles*) and set it on the\n"
"operation types, as explained in ``stock_capture``.\n"
"\n"
"Barcodes on master data:\n"
"\n"
"- Products: *Barcode* of the product.\n"
"- Locations: *Barcode* of the location (multi-location setting).\n"
"- Packagings: barcode of a unit of the product (several units of measure\n"
"  setting), e.g. *Pack of 6*.\n"
"- Lots, serial numbers and packages: their name is their barcode.\n"
"\n"
"The tiles of the *Barcodes* menu are barcode actions (*Inventory >\n"
"Configuration > Barcode Actions*): the window action or method they\n"
"open, the records they count and the barcode that opens them from the\n"
"menu. Select them and use *Print barcodes* to get a sheet with their\n"
"Code128 barcodes.\n"
"\n"
"Usage\n"
"=====\n"
"\n"
"Open the barcode screen from:\n"
"\n"
"1. The *Barcodes* menu: choose a tile (Receipts, Deliveries, Internal\n"
"   Transfers, Inventory, Operations) or read the barcode of a tile.\n"
"2. The cards of *Inventory > Overview*: read on any ready transfer of\n"
"   the operation type, list its transfers ready to read or start a new\n"
"   unplanned transfer.\n"
"3. The *Scan* button of a transfer, a batch transfer or, with\n"
"   ``stock_barcodes_mrp``, a manufacturing order.\n"
"\n"
"The screen keeps what you read until it is captured, and the session\n"
"survives the navigation for two days.\n"
"\n"
"**Reading.** Read in any order (free mode) or follow the pending card\n"
"proposed (guided mode). A product adds one unit (a packaging, its\n"
"quantity; a weight or GS1 barcode, its quantity); a tracked product\n"
"waits for its lot unless the profile takes it from the stock; a location\n"
"sets the source (or the destination, depending on the step); a package\n"
"with stock moves with all its content, another package becomes the\n"
"destination package. The message tells what was read and the line below\n"
"what the screen waits for. Readings that cannot be captured play an\n"
"error sound and say why: wrong product, lot or location for the card,\n"
"product not demanded, quantity not available in the location, or over\n"
"the demand (*Capture anyway* captures it).\n"
"\n"
"**Manual entry.** The keyboard button makes the fields editable;\n"
"*Confirm* captures them. With manual confirmation in the profile every\n"
"reading waits for *Confirm*, and repeated readings can add up.\n"
"\n"
"**Cards.** The pending operations or detailed operations of the\n"
"document, sorted by location. Tap a card to fill the screen from it. Its\n"
"buttons capture what is left, undo what was captured, leave a detailed\n"
"operation without capturing it or close an operation with or without\n"
"backorder. The eye button switches between pending and captured cards\n"
"and the list button shows the captured detailed operations, which can be\n"
"removed.\n"
"\n"
"**Other tools.** Product information (stock by location, on hand,\n"
"incoming, outgoing, forecasted) and selection of a source or destination\n"
"location with stock; new destination package and keeping it for the next\n"
"readings; serial numbers entered in the detailed operations of the\n"
"product; registering the barcode of a new packaging.\n"
"\n"
"**Validate** validates the document with the captured quantities,\n"
"putting it in a package first when the profile asks for it, and goes\n"
"back to the transfers ready to read.\n"
"\n"
"**Inventory.** The *Inventory* tile counts the stock of the main\n"
"warehouse. Each reading adds to the counted quantity of the location\n"
"read (or replaces it, depending on the profile); serial numbers count\n"
"one unit each. Cards show what you counted or what is pending, with\n"
"buttons to add, remove or clear. *Apply* applies your counts with the\n"
"reason Odoo asks for.\n"
"\n"
"Known issues / Roadmap\n"
"======================\n"
"\n"
"- Reading with the camera of the device (``BarcodeView`` of Odoo 20.0).\n"
"- The sound and notification settings per user.\n"
"- 18.0 grouped the pending cards by any expression; 20.0 groups detailed\n"
"  operations by location and product only.\n"
"\n"
"Changelog\n"
"=========\n"
"\n"
"20.0.1.0.0 (2026-10-17)\n"
"-----------------------\n"
"\n"
"- [MIG] Rebuilt on ``stock_capture``: the option groups become capture\n"
"  profiles (migrated with their steps; fields of other modules are\n"
"  migrated by them), the reading logic and the documents (transfers,\n"
"  operation types, batch transfers, inventories) move to the engine, and\n"
"  the screens read the real operations instead of copies. Batch\n"
"  transfers, part of ``stock`` in 20.0, are read without\n"
"  ``stock_barcodes_picking_batch``.\n"
"- [MIG] Quantities read on pending operations (``qty_picked``) and the\n"
"  backorder decisions are captured when migrating.\n"
"\n"
"18.0.1.6.0 (2026-10-02)\n"
"-----------------------\n"
"\n"
"- [ADD] Product information: a button next to the read product opens its\n"
"  on hand, incoming, outgoing and forecasted quantities and its stock in\n"
"  each location, ordered by the removal strategy (reversed on\n"
"  receptions). Tapping a location fills the screen location.\n"
"- [ADD] Buttons next to the source and destination locations list only\n"
"  the locations with stock to pick one, the destination ones in reverse\n"
"  order. On small screens the field icons replace these buttons.\n"
"\n"
"18.0.1.5.0 (2026-09-29)\n"
"-----------------------\n"
"\n"
"- [IMP] *Replace quantity on each reading* (``no_increase_qty_done``)\n"
"  now also applies to inventories: a reading is added to the counted\n"
"  quantity unless it is set. *Accumulate read quantity* is renamed to\n"
"  *Accumulate repeated readings* and adds one unit (or packaging) when\n"
"  the same item is read again before a manual confirmation. The\n"
"  migration keeps the inventory behavior of each database and leaves the\n"
"  new accumulation disabled.\n"
"- [FIX] Confirming a counted inventory line edited from the list added\n"
"  its quantity again (doubling it) when readings were added; the edited\n"
"  line now always replaces its counted quantity.\n"
"- [FIX] Map the 15.0 ``move_lines`` value of *Source pending moves* to\n"
"  ``move_ids``.\n"
"- [REM] Remove the unused *Show all quantities* and *Allow direct\n"
"  partial delivery* options.\n"
"\n"
"18.0.1.3.0 (2026-07-08)\n"
"-----------------------\n"
"\n"
"- [FIX] Restore bus notifications broken by the 18.0 bus API: scanning\n"
"  an action barcode from the main menu (whose client-side scanner\n"
"  capture was never wired since the feature was introduced in 16.0), the\n"
"  \"transfer validated\" toast, the manual-edit toggle from a pending line\n"
"  and the ``display_notification()`` toasts (e.g. \"Lot is required\"),\n"
"  which were sent with a per-record notification type nobody subscribes\n"
"  to. Events are now sent to the scanning user only instead of a\n"
"  broadcast channel.\n"
"- [FIX] Notify only the most significant message per interaction.\n"
"  Reading a barcode triggers sequential lookups and checks that buffer\n"
"  intermediate messages (e.g. \"Manual entry OK\" before the availability\n"
"  check rejects the entry), and each one used to raise its own\n"
"  notification. Messages are now buffered on the wizard (last one wins,\n"
"  as the on-screen message field always behaved) and a single\n"
"  notification is sent when the read or the manual confirmation ends:\n"
"  always for errors, only in manual entry for informative messages, and\n"
"  for \"Manual entry OK\" only when the whole confirmation succeeded.\n"
"- [FIX] Assign serial numbers button: the core removed the\n"
"  stock.assign.serial wizard in 18.0 leaving\n"
"  stock.move.action_assign_serial() broken (missing\n"
"  stock.act_assign_serial_numbers action), so the button crashed. It now\n"
"  opens the detailed operations dialog of the pending move, where the\n"
"  core 18.0 generate-serials widget lives. Lines receiving a lot/serial\n"
"  in that dialog are counted as scanned and linked to the pending card,\n"
"  so generated serials show up on the barcode screen.\n"
"- [FIX] Show each barcode notification only once. The barcode views\n"
"  subscribed the same handler to two bus notification types, which leaks\n"
"  a listener on every render (the bus service maps subscriptions by\n"
"  callback), so each notification was displayed more and more times as\n"
"  the session went on.\n"
"- [FIX] Barcode action tile counters: the model-field check never\n"
"  matched (checked attributes on a string), so tiles counted all records\n"
"  of the model; named filters now count records matching the filter.\n"
"- [REF] Drop the ``python-barcode`` external dependency introduced by\n"
"  the 17.0 migration: barcode action images are rendered again with the\n"
"  core ``ir.actions.report.barcode()`` helper, as in 16.0.\n"
"- [REF] Remove pre-17.0 immediate-transfer leftovers, use\n"
"  ``_read_group`` aggregation, convert the report model to\n"
"  ``AbstractModel``, drop a duplicated ACL, replace deprecated ``t-esc``\n"
"  with ``t-out`` and add ``limit=1`` to singleton barcode lookups.\n"
"- [REF] Rename misspelled methods (``_set_message_info``,\n"
"  ``check_location_condition``, ``check_lot_condition``). The old names\n"
"  are kept as deprecated aliases; modules overriding them must move\n"
"  their override to the new names.\n"
"\n"
"18.0.1.1.0 (2026-06-22)\n"
"-----------------------\n"
"\n"
"- [ADD] New option *Show fixed dest. location* on barcode option groups.\n"
"  It shows, in the pending moves list, the destination location already\n"
"  planned on the stock move line (for a fixed putaway, destination\n"
"  without storage category), and makes a scan reuse that move line\n"
"  keeping its destination instead of duplicating it at the generic\n"
"  picking destination. It never recomputes the putaway strategy.\n"
"\n"
"11.0.1.1.0 (2019-09-24)\n"
"-----------------------\n"
"\n"
"- [ADD] New feature. User can uses barcode interface in picking\n"
"  operations.\n"
"\n"
"13.0.1.1.1 (2021-02-06)\n"
"-----------------------\n"
"\n"
"- [ADD] New feature. Add option to get lots automatically based on\n"
"  removal strategy in inventory.\n"
"\n"
"14.0.1.0.0 (2021-04-05)\n"
"-----------------------\n"
"\n"
"- [ADD] New feature. Add security for users.\n"
"\n"
"16.0.1.0.0 (2025-01-23)\n"
"-----------------------\n"
"\n"
"- [IMP] Improved views to optimize navigation and functionality.\n"
"  Intuitive and mobile-friendly views. Visual improvement of the main\n"
"  view accessed from the Barcodes menu.\n"
"- [ADD] New feature. Barcode reading to barcode actions. Generate PDF\n"
"  document for the barcodes of the selected barcode actions.\n"
"\n"
"Bug Tracker\n"
"===========\n"
"\n"
"Bugs are tracked on `GitHub Issues <https://github.com/OCA/stock-logistics-"
"barcode/issues>`_.\n"
"In case of trouble, please check there if your issue has already been "
"reported.\n"
"If you spotted it first, help us to smash it by providing a detailed and "
"welcomed\n"
"`feedback <https://github.com/OCA/stock-logistics-barcode/issues/new?"
"body=module:%20stock_barcodes%0Aversion:"
"%2020.0%0A%0A**Steps%20to%20reproduce**%0A-%20..."
"%0A%0A**Current%20behavior**%0A%0A**Expected%20behavior**>`_.\n"
"\n"
"Do not contact contributors directly about support or help with technical "
"issues.\n"
"\n"
